<%@ Page Title="Emergency Procurement" Language="C#" MasterPageFile="~/MasterPages/Site.Master" %>
<asp:Content ID="Content1" ContentPlaceHolderID="MainContent" runat="server">
<section class="public-page"><div class="public-hero"><div class="site-container"><span class="public-kicker"><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation"></i> Emergency procurement</span><h1>Machine breakdowns need a <span>clear next step.</span></h1><p>The emergency request path is designed for urgent industrial spare-part requirements where the requester needs to describe the machine problem, part requirement and procurement priority.</p><div class="public-actions"><a class="public-button orange" href="~/Account/Register.aspx" runat="server">Start with Portal Registration</a><a class="public-button" href="~/Public/HowItWorks.aspx" runat="server">See the Workflow</a></div></div></div>
<section class="public-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="public-section-head"><span class="public-kicker">Emergency path</span><h2>Capture the information that matters first.</h2><p>The visitor page explains the process; the authenticated portal can later collect the actual request.</p></div><div class="public-grid"><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-industry"></i></div><h3>Machine information</h3><p>Identify the machine or equipment involved in the breakdown.</p></article><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-barcode"></i></div><h3>Part requirement</h3><p>Provide an OEM part number, machine name or available specification.</p></article><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-gauge-high"></i></div><h3>Urgency</h3><p>Record the emergency priority so the request can follow the appropriate workflow.</p></article><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-location-dot"></i></div><h3>Plant location</h3><p>Provide the relevant location for supplier and technician discovery.</p></article><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-invoice"></i></div><h3>Quotation path</h3><p>Move the requirement into supplier quotation and comparison when applicable.</p></article><article class="public-card"><div class="public-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-list-check"></i></div><h3>Status tracking</h3><p>Keep the request organized through defined status changes in the application.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="public-section alt"><div class="site-container"><div class="public-note"><strong>Important:</strong> this is a project demonstration. The displayed emergency workflow does not promise a real-world response time or emergency dispatch service.</div></div></section></section>
</asp:Content>